Z||000000||Bill 88||10-17-2000||02:48 PM||||I had removed the engine from my 88 several months ago and ust now got it back in.  I have a wire that I thought went to the trunk lid.  When it is attached I have a 12volt short to ground.  The only thing I can think of it is that I have another ground wire attached to the 12volt side . How many wires go to the starter? 2 or 3(I know, I should have drawn out and labeled all wires in the engine compartment)||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||10-17-2000||05:31 PM||||Not sure this helps answer your question, but...<P>If I'm not mistaken, there are only two connections to the rear deck lid.  One, on the RHS, is a 4-pin connector that provides electric trunk release and trunk light.  The other, on the LHS, is a single black wire that provides a ground for the deck lid (RF shielding function).<P>  ||||reg||3
Z||000002||wilburt||10-18-2000||06:21 AM||||Bill 88, There is a black wire that connects to the deck lid, goes into the main wire harness, comes back out, and then connects to a trans. to engine stud bolt. This wire will reach down to the starter, and has an end that will connect to the starter. It does NOT go on the starter. It connects to the stud bolt,(ground). <P>Three connections on the starter. A small wire to small terminal, two wires connected with one end go to large terminal, and the battery positive cable end, also to the large terminal. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||10-19-2000||08:33 AM||||"two wires connected with one end go to large terminal"<P>hmm, I'm not sure if I have a wire like that down there... but I do have 2 wires w/ one end that goto the small terminal, the main + wire going to the big terminal, and a grounding wire up under the shorter starter bolt. hope it helps.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bill 88||10-19-2000||03:02 PM||||Thanks, I will try that this weekend.  Hopefully it will fire up and I can go cruising(sp??).||||reg||1
Z||000005||PatrickB||10-20-2000||07:52 PM||||While were on the topic...<BR>Ive been going through fixing up all my ground wires and apparently the person before did not like grounds because he either cut or  disconnected a bunch of them.  I though I had most of them but I found another one today.  Its connected on the driver side wall towards the bottom and near the firewall.  Its connected right by where the metal brake line comes into the engine compartment.  Anyone know where the other end connects to?<P>Thanks.||||reg||12
